# Modus Web Components + Next.js Integration Guide

## 🎯 Overview

This project integrates **Modus Web Components** with **Next.js 15** using React 19. The integration follows specific patterns to handle server-side rendering, client-side interactivity, and proper component registration.

## 📦 Package Dependencies

### Required Packages

```json
{
  "@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-react": "^1.0.0-react19",
  "@trimble-oss/modus-icons": "^1.17.1"
}
```

### Key Points

- **React 19 Compatibility**: Uses the `-react19` variant of the Modus package
- **Icons Package**: Separate package for Modus icon fonts
- **Version Alignment**: Ensure React 19 compatibility across all Modus packages

## 🏗️ Architecture Patterns

### 1. Provider Pattern for Component Registration

**File**: `app/components/ModusProvider.tsx`

```tsx
"use client";

import "@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-react/modus-wc-styles.css";

export default function ModusProvider({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode;
}) {
  return <>{children}</>;
}
```

**Critical Notes**:

- ✅ **Client Component**: Must be `"use client"` directive
- ✅ **CSS Import**: Imports Modus styles directly
- ✅ **No useEffect**: React package handles component registration automatically
- ❌ **No defineCustomElements**: Not needed with React wrapper package

### 2. Layout Integration

**File**: `app/layout.tsx`

```tsx
import ModusProvider from "./components/ModusProvider";

export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode;
}) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        <ModusProvider>{children}</ModusProvider>
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

**Critical Notes**:

- ✅ **Wraps All Pages**: Provider must wrap all app content
- ✅ **Server Component**: Layout remains server-side
- ✅ **Single Provider**: Only one ModusProvider needed

### 3. Client Component Pattern for Interactivity

**File**: `app/components/ModusButtonDemo.tsx`

```tsx
"use client";

import { ModusWcButton } from "@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-react";

export default function ModusButtonDemo() {
  const handleButtonClick = () => {
    console.log("Modus button clicked!");
    alert("Modus button clicked!");
  };

  return (
    <ModusWcButton
      color="primary"
      variant="filled"
      size="md"
      onButtonClick={handleButtonClick}
    >
      <i className="modus-icons text-lg mr-2">apps</i>
      Test Modus Button
    </ModusWcButton>
  );
}
```

**Critical Notes**:

- ✅ **Client Component**: Must be `"use client"` for event handlers
- ✅ **React Import**: Use `ModusWcButton` from React package, not raw web component
- ✅ **Event Handlers**: Can use `onButtonClick` and other event props
- ❌ **No Raw Web Components**: Don't use `<modus-wc-button>` directly

## 🎨 CSS Integration

### 1. Icons CSS Import

**File**: `app/globals.css`

```css
@import url("https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@trimble-oss/modus-icons@1.17.0/dist/field-systems/fonts/modus-icons.css");
@import "tailwindcss";
```

**Critical Notes**:

- ✅ **Import Order**: Icons CSS must come BEFORE Tailwind CSS
- ✅ **CDN Import**: Uses CDN for icon fonts
- ✅ **Field Systems**: Uses field-systems icon set (623 icons)
- ❌ **Wrong Order**: `@import` rules must precede all other CSS rules

### 2. Icon Usage Pattern

```tsx
<i className="modus-icons text-lg mr-2">apps</i>
```

**Critical Notes**:

- ✅ **Class Name**: Always use `modus-icons` class
- ✅ **Icon Names**: Use exact icon names (e.g., `apps`, `user_permissions`)
- ✅ **Styling**: Use `fontSize` and `color` for customization
- ✅ **Spacing**: Add `marginRight` for text spacing

## 🔧 TypeScript Configuration

### 1. Type Declarations

**File**: `types/modus.d.ts`

```typescript
declare namespace JSX {
  interface IntrinsicElements {
    "modus-wc-button": {
      color?: "primary" | "secondary" | "tertiary" | "warning" | "danger";
      variant?: "filled" | "outlined" | "borderless";
      size?: "xs" | "sm" | "md" | "lg";
      shape?: "rectangle" | "square" | "circle";
      type?: "button" | "submit" | "reset";
      disabled?: boolean;
      "full-width"?: boolean;
      pressed?: boolean;
      "custom-class"?: string;
      onButtonClick?: (event: CustomEvent) => void;
      children?: React.ReactNode;
    };
  }
}
```

### 2. TypeScript Config

**File**: `tsconfig.json`

```json
{
  "include": [
    "next-env.d.ts",
    "**/*.ts",
    "**/*.tsx",
    ".next/types/**/*.ts",
    "types/**/*.d.ts"
  ]
}
```

**Critical Notes**:

- ✅ **Include Types**: Must include `types/**/*.d.ts` in tsconfig
- ✅ **Component Props**: Define all available props and events
- ✅ **Event Types**: Use `CustomEvent` for component events

## 🚨 Common Pitfalls & Solutions

### 1. Server/Client Component Issues

**❌ Problem**: Event handlers in server components

```
Error: Event handlers cannot be passed to Client Component props.
```

**✅ Solution**: Create separate client components for interactivity

```tsx
// ❌ Wrong - Server component with event handler
export default function Page() {
  return <ModusWcButton onButtonClick={() => {}}>Click me</ModusWcButton>;
}

// ✅ Correct - Client component for interactivity
("use client");
export default function InteractiveButton() {
  return <ModusWcButton onButtonClick={() => {}}>Click me</ModusWcButton>;
}
```

### 2. CSS Import Order Issues

**❌ Problem**: CSS parsing errors

```
@import rules must precede all rules aside from @charset and @layer statements
```

**✅ Solution**: Put all `@import` statements at the top of CSS files

```css
/* ✅ Correct order */
@import url("https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@trimble-oss/modus-icons@1.17.0/dist/field-systems/fonts/modus-icons.css");
@import "tailwindcss";

/* ❌ Wrong - @import after other rules */
:root {
  --color: red;
}
@import "tailwindcss";
```

### 3. Component Registration Issues

**❌ Problem**: Components not rendering

```
Module not found: Can't resolve '@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-react/loader'
```

**✅ Solution**: Use React package directly, no loader needed

```tsx
// ❌ Wrong - Trying to use loader
import { defineCustomElements } from "@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-react/loader";

// ✅ Correct - Import components directly
import { ModusWcButton } from "@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-react";
```

### 4. Icon Not Displaying

**❌ Problem**: Icons show as text or don't appear

**✅ Solution**: Check CSS import and class name

```tsx
// ✅ Correct icon usage
<i className="modus-icons">apps</i>

// ❌ Wrong - Missing class or wrong name
<i>apps</i>
<i className="modus-icon">apps</i>
```

